<title>USA: Brent crude loses ground in late US paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude loses ground in late US paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea benchmark Brent crude oil lost ground in late U.S. paper trading, traders said.</p>
<p>A series of August Brent partial cargoes traded at $17.70 and $17.73 a barrel, down from the IPE settlement of $17.80.</p>
<p>July/August Brent changed hands twice at minus 29 cents a barrel and once at minus 30 cents, down from minus 25 cents earlier in the day.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
